.TH NAVI-UPDATE 1 2026-11-27 Navi "Navi Manual"
.nh
.SH NAME
navi-update \- update Navi
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B navi-update
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-y ]
.br
.B navi-update \-\-undo
.SH DESCRIPTION
Updates Navi to the newest version on GitHub.
It shows what will change and asks once before updating.
Answer
.B d
to see every change first.
.PP
Files you have edited are kept.
Navi's new version is saved next to them with
.B .navi-new
added to the name.
.PP
Programs like dwm and st are built before anything is changed.
If a build fails, your files and programs are left as they were.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would change, then stop.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Update without asking.
.TP
.B \-\-undo
Put back the last update.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.navi-backup-*/
Files replaced by each update.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/navi-update/
Build output, for when a build fails.
